  "summary": "At a San Diego District 2 candidate forum, Nicole Crosby and Richard Bailey debated city budget, homelessness, and ALPRs. Crosby said she distrusts Flock, the city's ALPR vendor, while Bailey argued for keeping the technology with more guardrails, such as publishing license plate numbers in the search log and shortening data retention from a month to a week.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I don't trust the entities that are controlling that information, but I do trust our local San Diego police officers... we need to make sure that our communities are safe and they're not being overrun by big brother Flock",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    },
    {
      "quote": "He proposed that the public database that logs ALPR searches should include license plate numbers, so residents can see if they are actively being surveilled. He also said he would like to see the city delete data after a week rather than a month.",
      "paragraph_idx": 23
    }
  ],
